Topological quantum hashing with the icosahedral group

The set of programs provides an object-oriented implementation of the
algorithm introduced in the manuscript M. Burrello, H. Xu,
G. Mussardo, Xin Wan, arXiv:0903.1497. This is an efficient algorithm
to hash any single qubit gate (or unitary matrix) into a braid of
Fibonacci anyons represented by a product of icosahedral group
elements. The algorithm relies on the structure of the icosahedral
group, the largest finite subgroup of $SU(2)$.

